                <pb facs="0302" n="200" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg200"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.73/173: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Morgan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rio de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-05-01T13:00:00-03:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 1, 1919, 1
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received July 3, 5.05
                            p.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>In spite of representations to [omission] and the good will of Brazilian Foreign
                    Office the Western Telegraph line’s opposition to the registration of the
                    Central and South American Telegraph Company’s Cuban concession continues. If
                    this opposition were removed the matter would probably go forward
                    satisfactorily.</p>
                <p>Cannot steps be taken in London to remove the unjustified impediments which this
                    British Company is placing in the way of a legitimate and necessary American
                    enterprise? My patience and resources here are about exhausted.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Morgan</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
